# ESP32 serial policy (locked)

All code that opens `/dev/ttyUSB0` (or ESP32 serial) must use `esp32_serial.py` — not ad-hoc link flags.

## Required pattern

1. **Configure before connect**: `configure_esp32_link(link)` or `connect_esp32()`
2. **Never** set `_skip_tof_probe_at_connect`, `_allow_dtr_reset`, `_port_wait_sec` inline elsewhere
3. **Prepare before live control**: `prepare_esp32_for_live_control(link)` after connect + CPD
4. **Throttle head P/T serial** to `ESP32_SERIAL_SEND_HZ` (30 Hz) — never send at 100 Hz
5. **One program per port** — `start_robot.py` and `test_head_servos.py` cannot run together
6. **Robot runtime**: ESP32 connects in background; camera/vision start first (`robot_eyes.py`)
7. **No DTR reset** on reconnect (`ESP32_ALLOW_DTR_RESET = False`)
8. **Reconnect** on serial loss via `_schedule_servo_reconnect` in `robot_eyes.py`

## Constants (in `esp32_serial.py`)

| Constant | Value | Why |
|----------|-------|-----|
| `ESP32_SERIAL_SEND_HZ` | 30 | Prevents command backlog / delayed servo response |
| `ESP32_PORT_WAIT_SEC` | 45 | USB hotplug tolerance |
| `ESP32_SKIP_TOF_PROBE_AT_CONNECT` | True | Fast ready; ToF polls in worker |
| `ESP32_ALLOW_DTR_RESET` | False | Avoid reboot + stale queued commands |

## Do not change without user approval

- Do not revert to blocking ESP32 connect before camera
- Do not increase serial send rate above 30 Hz for head servos
- Do not remove `flush_pending_commands()` before interactive/tracking control
- Do not re-enable USB webcam paths (CSI Picamera2 only)
